   "page": 3,
   "description": "Off-line buck LED driver. A bridge rectifies the AC line onto a capacitor that holds the high-voltage rail. The LED string hangs from that rail, and the inductor returns its lower end to the DRAIN pin. While the internal switch is on, current ramps through LEDs, inductor and switch to ground; while it is off, the freewheel diode carries the inductor current back into the rail end of the string. VDD has only its bypass capacitor.",
